\pard\sb360\sa180{\b\f0\fs36\ulth Request for Mod Authors using xEdit}\par
\pard\sa180{\f0\fs24 If you share your mods on Nexus Mods and use xEdit as a major component in development, please consider donating a small share of your Donation Points (DP) to ElminsterAU to support the ongoing development of this tool. The recommended donation is ~10%.}\par
\pard\sa180{\f0\fs24 xEdit is crucial to our shared modding community and your contribution - no matter the size - is invaluable and deeply appreciated.}\par
\pard\sb360\sa180{\b\f0\fs36\ulth What's New in xEdit 4.1.5r?}\par
\pard\sb300\sa180{\b\f0\fs32\ulth TL;DR}\par
\pard\sa180{\f0\fs24 About 1,250 commits since 4.1.5q. The Merged Patch is rebuilt as a three-way merge, Create Delta Patch and Merge into Master now round-trip, world space offset tables are written on save, Morrowind gains NAME links and Referenced By, and hundreds of crashes, data-loss paths and malformed-archive failures are fixed. Underneath, the engine no longer depends on the user interface or on one global game, and xEdit builds with Delphi 13.}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Key highlights}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Merged Patch - entries are now merged three-way against each plugin's own master, so a plugin only counts where it actually changed something}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Create Delta Patch and Merge into Master - a delta patch between two versions of a module, merged back into the first, now gives the second}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab World spaces - valid OFST tables, and CLSZ on Fallout 4 and later, are written on save by default}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Morrowind - NAME references are links, Referenced By works, and Check for Errors knows Morrowind's identity rules (Morrowind is still view only in this release)}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Saving - a failed save no longer leaves a damaged file or reads as saved}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Closing and cancelling - the editor stays safe when you close it, or press keys, while something is running, and a Windows session end behaves like a normal close}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab BSArch - full PlayStation GNMF archive support, Bethesda's texture chunking, no more forced texture compression, and malformed archives are refused instead of crashing}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Definitions - Fallout 76 updated to HEDR 266 and Form Version 209, Starfield soundbank names reworked, and many fixes across all games}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Contributors}\par
\pard\sa180{\f0\fs24 ElminsterAU, robertgk2017, Jonathan Ostrus (jbostrus), eckserah, fireundubh, sheson, and thanks to Cobb for assistance.}\par
\pard\sb300\sa180{\b\f0\fs32\ulth Major Features}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Merged Patch}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A plugin's entry is now taken only where that plugin changed it against its own master; if two plugins change the same entry, the later one wins}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Identical additions made by two plugins count once; if they differ, the later plugin's addition wins}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A compatibility patch is compared with the merge of its masters, so its removals and reversals count}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Entries are paired by what they are, across changes of count and between entries that share a key}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Now merges Starfield's nested NPC perks and container items, a Fallout 76 NPC's inventory, and Oblivion NPC and race spells}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A delta patch can be merged; a plugin and its own Compare To copy are not merged with each other}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The keyword lists, which never merged, were removed}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Create Delta Patch, Compare To and Merge into Master}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A delta patch between two versions of a module, merged into the first with Merge into Master, gives the second, in either order}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Create Delta Patch ignores Allow Make Partial, and no longer runs after a failed or terminated delta load}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Compare To and Create Delta Patch work against a Starfield update module}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A Starfield delta patch that would change the module's type is refused with a message before its masters are loaded}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A record created in a delta patch belongs to the delta patch's module from the start, and Clean Masters keeps that module and its masters}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A file loaded through Compare To can never be saved}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth World space offset tables}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A valid OFST cell-offset table is written for every world space on save, by default, with a new Options checkbox; on Oblivion only in the file that creates the world space}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab On Fallout 4 and later the CLSZ cell-size grid is written with it}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The in-memory tables are updated too, so the View tab shows what was written, and a stale table can no longer be saved}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Morrowind (view only in this release)}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab NAME references behave like FormID links: leveled list entries, a reference's base record, cell names and the other record references}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Referenced By tracks NAME references, and a note says when the list may be incomplete}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab An INFO is identified by its topic and INAM}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Check for Errors reports a record's shared key, a bad grid and a blocked identity, and checks leveled lists for cycles using the game's own lookup rules}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A faction's relations are shown as reaction and faction name}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Records and references are counted and placed the way the file holds them}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Views and windows}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Right Click > Edit in the View tab now opens every editable field: the single-line dialog for fields with an in-place editor, the multi-line editor for the rest (contributed by robertgk2017)}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Add a clipboard copy menu to the View tab's column header (#1495, contributed by Jonathan Ostrus)}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Hiding is now per view rather than global, and Hide Never Show is a setting}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The Options dialog shows the collapse options as a grouped checkbox tree}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The View tab refreshes itself when it goes stale, and its header keeps the theme's look with only its captions coloured}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A visible zebra stripe on dark styles, and the window colour on the spreadsheets under a VCL style}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Referenced By now uses the same Virtual TreeView as the rest of the editor, and Ctrl+C copies the selected records' load order FormIDs (Ctrl+Alt+C their names)}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Show the enchantment in Oblivion's spreadsheets and the enchantment and amount in Skyrim's weapon spreadsheet; Skyrim's spreadsheet keyword dialog appears again}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Light and medium plugins}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Compact FormIDs takes a goal: light or medium}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Renumber and Inject hold a light- or medium-flagged file to its flag's range}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Detect OblivionESL.dll as light plugin support for Oblivion, and what Daytripper4.dll enables on Fallout 4 VR}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Engine}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The conflict walk, the editor's data operations (Copy Into, Renumber, Clean Masters, Merge into Master, Quick Auto Clean and more) and Create Delta Patch moved out of the user interface into the engine}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The engine no longer has a current game or context: every record reaches its own game definition and context}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Saves are loaded through a save context on top of the game context, and are no longer treated as plugins}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The resource cache is built on its own thread while plugins load}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab xEdit now builds with Delphi 13 (Community Edition included)}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Virtual TreeView, JCL, vcl-styles-utils, JsonDataObjects and lz4-delphi updated from their upstream projects}\par
\pard\sb300\sa180{\b\f0\fs32\ulth Bugfixes}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Saving}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A failed save no longer commits, reads as saved, or leaves a file behind, and a failed Save As keeps the target's bytes}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A plugin whose save file cannot be created is reported and the rest of the batch goes on; if the save was part of closing, the close stops}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Keep a file's edits when its write resets the modified state}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Only the editor's own save marks a plugin saved; no script export does}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Keep a replaced plugin's time exactly, and report a failed update of it}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Remove a .seq file the plugin no longer needs}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Fix main records losing all their subrecords when storage was invalidated during initialisation}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Masters, FormIDs and copying}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Reference the game master for a hardcoded FormID in a module without the extended range}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Renumber skips FormIDs other files injected, and a FormID change that does not fit the target's slot is refused}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Refuse a new record, or a changed FormID, with ObjectID 000}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Sort Masters handles a master listed twice and a master whose index among its type changes}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Refuse a module that is its own master}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Cleanup Injected skips and reports a cleanup whose target already holds the record}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Follow load order for a record's winner and its next master}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Copy no more entries than an array's maximum, and report lists over it in Check for Errors}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A record a script assigns to itself keeps its data}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Copy to Selected and Copy multiple rows to selected records no longer write into a record that is not editable (a game master's, a Compare To copy's, the hardcoded file's), which could empty its keyword and other lists; with no target left they show a message}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Dropping or row-copying one plugin's Master Files onto another file header, or dropping a whole file header onto another, no longer writes a master with an empty name, which left a plugin that could not be loaded}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Loading and caches}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Rebuild a reference cache that cannot be read or does not match its file, and save it atomically}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Refuse a strings file, a record or compressed data that runs past its end}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Skip .git folders when listing a loose data folder}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Unregister a failed plugin's records from its masters}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Closing, cancelling and background work}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The editor is safe against close requests, shortcuts and timers arriving while a nested operation runs; a close during a cancellable operation asks first, then stops it}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A Windows session end shows the same save dialog as a normal close, and Cancel refuses it}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A script can not start while the background loader runs}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Crash fixes for closing with a given tab active and for a close during reference building}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A force cancel waits until Add Masters, Clean Masters, Sort Masters or a Change FormID has reached a safe point}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The game link and Oblivion's Pluggy link retry a read that fails for a moment, and keep running after a refused close}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Checks and display}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Conflict results: FO3 / FNV navmesh triangle edges are compared, and landscape normals are Benign only when the height map is identical}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Check for Errors no longer loops on a cyclic parent chain or NPC template chain}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Fix an access violation in condition-alias resolution for INFO records}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Stop offering Remove on a record's Record Header}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The View tab's column header menu no longer offers Remove on a file header, which left a plugin that could not be saved}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Remove in the Referenced By tab no longer removes a record of a file that can not be edited, such as the game master's; a selection that includes one is refused with a message}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Visible When Distant and Not Visible When Distant in the navigation tree no longer change a reference of a file that can not be edited, such as the game master's; a selection that includes one is refused with a message}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Cleanup Injected no longer changes a record of a file that can not be edited, such as a Compare To copy's}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Filtering the Referenced By list no longer leaves a row selected that you did not select, so a following command can not act on the wrong record}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A double at its maximum or minimum shows as Default or Min}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The navigation tree no longer sometimes paints its last row a second time on the empty row below it}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Fix a RichEdit EOutOfResources error when adding lines (contributed by sheson)}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Command line and unattended runs}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab An unattended run logs a failure and exits non-zero instead of showing a dialog}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab -autoload and -autoexit work in script mode; a missing or unreadable script fails the run}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab -autoload and -autoexit work in MasterUpdate, MasterRestore and OnamUpdate}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab MasterUpdate, MasterRestore and setESM start again, -SortAndCleanMasters is accepted, and a plugin can be named by full path or with .ghost}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab A -M: My Games path gets its trailing backslash}\par
