\pard\sb300\sa180{\b\f0\fs32\ulth Partial Form Support}\par
\pard\sa180{\f0\fs24 Initial support for Partial Forms has been implemented:}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Records marked as Partial Form are ignored in conflict status determination.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The Partial Form Flag is correctly displayed as a Record Flag on all Records that support it.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The Partial Form Flag can only be set on records where it is likely safe to do so.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Setting the Partial Form Flag will remove all subrecords except EditorID.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab Removing the Partial Form Flag will restore the subrecords from the highest visible master.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li360\tx360{\f0\fs24 \bullet\tab The -AllowMakePartial parameter, which only works if you know what you are doing, will allow QAC to mark ITM records that can be Partial Forms as such, if they can't be removed because they have children.}\par
\pard\sb240\sa180{\b\f0\fs28\ulth Warning}\par
\pard\sa180{\f0\fs24 The safety of using Partial Forms in different contexts in the various game engines is still under exploration. Marking a record as Partial Form might result in engine bugs and unexpected behaviour.}\par
